A-2. The only relevant post-cutoff hit in the delta window:
     arXiv:2608.26407v1, submitted 2026-08-26, G. Scala & C. Lupo,
     "Recovery-Free CHSH Nonlocality with Particle Loss".
     https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26407 (accessed 2026-08-28)
     Claims (from abstract): for flagged erasure and survival probability
     eta>1/2, measurements asymptotically approach the quantum maximum 2*sqrt(2);
     for eta<=1/2 CHSH violation is impossible under both loss models; explicit
     recovery-free Dicke-state protocols violate CHSH for eta>1/sqrt(2) (one
     excitation) and eta>eta_G=(sqrt(5)-1)/2 asymptotically.
     Metric: NONE — quantum-capacity / particle-loss result on standard QM with
     lossy channels. Model class: no hidden variables, no measurement
     dependence, no TV distance of any kind.
     Overlap with OUR claims (i) per-setting TV metric F, (ii) exact closed
     forms/curves/cap/S<=2+8F, (iii) NS-silence: NONE. Class iii (unrelated
     context). No citation required.

A-3. Catalogue additions — pre-cutoff papers the first sweep missed (all
     verified at abstract level this sweep; none overlaps claims (i)–(iii);
     none requires citation in the paper):
  - arXiv:2512.17024v2 (2025-12-22), Boulle & Franzmann, "Subsystems
    (in)dependence in GIE proposals". https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.17024
    AQFT analysis of subsystem independence for gravitationally-induced-
    entanglement proposals; CHSH/Tsirelson appears only as a side case study
    (Tsirelson bound persists for a symmetrized CHSH observable when algebras
    fail to commute). Class iii, no MD metric.
  - arXiv:2601.14316v2 (v2 2026-08-02), Cafiero, Molinari & Hance, "The burden
    of Fundamentality: Metaphysical ambiguities and the issue of
    Superdeterminism". https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.14316
    Conceptual (naive vs metaphysical superdeterminism; Invariant Set Theory).
    Class iii, no metric.
  - arXiv:2605.29589v1 (2026-05-28), G. Beck, "Bell's theorem: why probability
    factorisation fails". https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.29589
    Sequential single-spin counterfactual argument; conceptual. Class iii, no
    metric.
  - arXiv:2604.00311v1 (2026-03-31), M. Waegell, "On measurement,
    superdeterminism, free will, and contextuality". https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.00311
    Formalizes what "nonsuperdeterministic" requires of a theory; conceptual.
    Class iii, no metric.
  - arXiv:2607.18383v1 (2026-07-20), Di Biagio & de la Hamette, "Adlam's Frame:
    comment on 'Wigner's Frame'". https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18383
    Critique of a QRF-based resolution of extended-Wigner's-friend no-go
    theorems; conceptual. Class iii, no metric.
  - arXiv:2411.11397v2 (v2 2026-05-28), Kunjwal & Oreshkov, "Generalizing Bell
    nonlocality without global causal assumptions". https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.11397
    Introduces "antinomicity" for single-round-communication cyclic-causation
    scenarios; the abstract calls it "an instance of fine-tuning" but for
    classical models avoiding time-travel antinomies — NOT measurement
    dependence. Class iii, no MD metric.
  - arXiv:2608.06359v1 (2026-08-06), Djordjevic et al., "Bell nonlocality from
    twisted statistics". https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06359
    CHSH violation from noncommutative (Moyal-plane) scalar QFT; no MD metric.
    Class iii.
  - arXiv:2608.20926v1 (2026-08-21), "Finite Weyl polynomials and the approach
    to Tsirelson's bound in relativistic scalar quantum field theory".
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.20926 — TITLE-LEVEL ONLY, not read in depth;
    QFT bounds on the Tsirelson bound, no MD metric expected from title.
    Class iii (title-level).
  - arXiv:2608.04128v1 (2026-08-04), "Quantum Contextuality and Entanglement-
    Free Grover Search in a Trapped-Ion Optical Qudit".
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04128 — TITLE-LEVEL ONLY; experimental
    contextuality. Class iii (title-level).

